WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.560
OK, you might remember this guy named William
Barr.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.109
He is the attorney general.

00:00:06.109 --> 00:00:10.320
After all, he's Donald Trump's hatchet man,
attorney general.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:17.030
And he up until yesterday had all but completely
disappeared from the public eye since he attended

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.450
that White House super spreader event for
Donald Trump.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:22.820
Supreme Court pick Amy CONI Barrett.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.220
That was that event which set in motion this
chain of coronavirus cases.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:33.740
Bar went missing for a while after that point
bar resurfaced yesterday to say without any

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:39.550
hesitation, at this point, there is no evidence
of widespread election fraud that would have

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:42.100
affected the election results in any way.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.290
Now, you still have people saying, well, what
about this one vote?

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.060
A dead person really did vote.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:57.030
The point is, there is no evidence at this
point of fraud of any materially significant

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.870
nature to the election.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:04.260
You also immediately had counter articles
coming out saying, no, BAH didn't clear everybody

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.260
of fraud.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:12.190
What Barr said is to date, there is no evidence
of materially significant election fraud.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:15.580
He said this in an interview yesterday with
the Associated Press.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:22.170
His exact statement was, quote, To date, to
date, we have not seen fraud on a scale that

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:25.659
could have affected a different outcome in
the election.

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:29.820
There has been one assertion that would be
systemic fraud, and that would be the claim

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:33.740
that machines were programed to skew the election
results.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:36.390
And the DHS and DOJ have looked into that.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:42.810
And so far, we haven't seen anything to substantiate
that as this was breaking.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:47.000
Donald Trump tweeting, quote, I hope everybody
is watching away.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:53.030
And right now, other media afraid to show
people are coming forward like never before.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:59.810
Large truck carrying hundreds of thousands
of fraudulent fake ballots to a voting center.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:02.729
Terrible save America.

00:02:02.729 --> 00:02:08.189
So at this point, Donald Trump's claims are
sort of a running parallel commentary that's

00:02:08.189 --> 00:02:11.310
completely divorced from all the facts on
the ground.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:15.641
And then immediately after William Barr said
this, there was speculation that Donald Trump

00:02:15.641 --> 00:02:22.000
was going to fire him because within moments
of that interview being published, a William

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.700
Barr was seen arriving at the White House
and the speculation was, oh, boy, Trump called

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.840
him in and he's going to fire him right now.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.359
That's not at all what was going on.

00:02:30.359 --> 00:02:35.269
That was a preplanned meeting with the chief
of staff, Mark Meadows.

00:02:35.269 --> 00:02:41.719
CNN's Caitlin Collins reporting that, quote,
Attorney General Barr is in the West Wing

00:02:41.719 --> 00:02:44.219
for a meeting with Mark Meadows.

00:02:44.219 --> 00:02:49.290
An official says the meeting was planned before
his interview with the Associated Press.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:55.579
Now, it certainly wouldn't be beyond Trump
to fire William Barr for saying this.

00:02:55.579 --> 00:02:58.599
That would actually be totally unsurprising.

00:02:58.599 --> 00:03:03.909
But the speculation that the timing of Barr
going to the White House after saying yesterday,

00:03:03.909 --> 00:03:08.779
no evidence of election fraud, that was mere
speculation.

00:03:08.779 --> 00:03:12.139
And he was actually there to meet with the
chief of staff, Mark Meadows.

00:03:12.139 --> 00:03:18.319
Now, there are all sorts of other things going
on involving the Justice Department, some

00:03:18.319 --> 00:03:24.139
not very good for Trump, which could have
been the reasons for William Barr or at least

00:03:24.139 --> 00:03:28.010
the subject matter of William Barr's meeting
with Chief of Staff Mark Meadows.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:04:07.229
Let's talk about one 

00:04:07.229 --> 00:04:19.090
of 

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:45.530
those next.

